week 4
-- tokenizer comparison --

-- our computers are not capable of understanding human language directly
-- this is why there exist models which understand or try to interpret human language 
-- such a model is known as language model
-- this model converts human language into tokens
-- in a sentence every word is converted into a token and then token ids are created 
-- the model processes those ids 
-- For each sentence the program prints the token pieces, these ids are in vector format which helps the computer to understand


-- what i did 

I compared three tokenizers on English, Telugu, and Hindi text. The output showed how each splits text into tokens and counts them.

Files: tokenizer_comparison.py, requirements.txt
